<title>UK: ABP well placed for growth.</title>
<headline>ABP well placed for growth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Associated British Ports Plc, Britain's biggest port group, said on Wednesday it was well placed to exploit the growth in home and world economies after reporting year profits of 93.5 million pounds.</p>
<p>Pre-tax profits for the year ended December 31 were up 5.8 percent after accounting for a three million pounds charge relating to the exit from an engineering joint venture. The total dividend payout was 7.75 pence.</p>
</text>
